# Genetic Admixture Modelling Pipeline (qpAdm)

An **auditable** workflow that takes a consumer DNA raw-data file, merges it with the
[Allen Ancient DNA Resource (AADR)](https://reich.hms.harvard.edu/allen-ancient-dna-resource-aadr-downloadable-genotypes-present-day-and-ancient-dna-data),
runs **classic ADMIXTOOLS qpAdm** on a model you define, and saves parsed results together
with every command, log, and failed or rejected run.

It is built around the South Asian **Indian Cline**, which is modelled with three ancestry
proxies:

| Proxy | Meaning |
|---|---|
| AASI-related | Deep South Asian lineage (Onge/AHG used as an imperfect surrogate) |
| Indus Periphery-related | Iran-related plus South Asian-related ancestry |
| Steppe_MLBA-related | Middle-to-Late Bronze Age Steppe-related ancestry |

> These are **analytical proxies**, not literal unadmixed ancestors, social categories, or
> language labels.

**This project is not a new ancestry algorithm.** The qpAdm statistics are unchanged
(ADMIXTOOLS does the computing). The contribution is the preparation, logging and
provenance layer around it. Related tools already exist, including
[ADMIXTOOLS 2](https://uqrmaie1.github.io/admixtools/),
qpAdm-wrapper, and ColabADMIXTOOLS. See the paper in
[`docs/`](docs/) for the full comparison.

